class.description:
Create a runtime with [method initialize], execute code with [method eval], and exchange values with [method set_global] and [method get_global].
[b]Basic usage[/b]
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var environment := PuertsEnvironment.new()
var backend := PuertsV8Backend.new()
var cache := PuertsStringNameUtf8Cache.new()

if environment.initialize(backend, cache) == OK:
	environment.set_global(&"answer", 42)
	var result := environment.eval("answer + 1", &"example.js")
	if result != null:
		print(result.to_float()) # 43.0
	environment.dispose()
[/codeblock]
[b]Script globals[/b]
	• [code]load_type(name)[/code] — Loads a Godot type.
	• [code]load_addon_type(name)[/code] — Loads a registered addon type.
	• [code]to_callable(function)[/code] — Converts a script function to a Godot [Callable].
	• [code]PLogger[/code] — Writes categorized logs, as shown below.
Use [method set_global] to expose additional objects or data to scripts.
[b]Logging[/b]
Each method takes a category ID and a message:
	• [b]Categories:[/b] Positive int32 IDs. Category [code]0[/code] is reserved for Puerts.
	• [b]Filtering:[/b] Defaults to [constant LOG_LEVEL_INFO]. Configure with [method set_log_level] and [method set_category_log_level].
	• [b]Output:[/b] Defaults to Godot output when no valid callback is configured. Register [method set_log_callback] before initialization to also capture initialization errors. See that method for a callback example.
[codeblock lang=javascript]
PLogger.trace(1, "Sending packet");
PLogger.debug(1, "Connected");
PLogger.info(2, "Player joined");
PLogger.warning(1, "Connection is slow");
PLogger.error(1, "Connection failed");
[/codeblock]
[b]Lifetime and threading[/b]
Keep a reference to the environment while using its script values or script-backed [Callable]s.
Use the environment, its values, and its [PuertsStringNameUtf8Cache] on the same thread.
[b]Web backend:[/b] [PuertsWebBackend] allows only one environment, which remains alive until page unload. [method dispose] and reinitialization are unsupported.
